{"availability":"available","full":"Zeptaz/hutch_resolve","name":"hutch_resolve","description":"hutch resolve: a customer complain resolution engine built for hutch","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-01T20:42:08Z","updated":"2026-10-04T06:50:10Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hutch-resolve.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://resolve.zeptaz.com/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:28.856Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:28.856Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:28.856Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T06:51:28.856Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Evidence-backed AI resolution for telecom customer complaints.","All data in this repository is synthetic. No HUTCH system, API, credential or real customer record is used or connected."],"features":["Four complaint types, six seeded cases (A–F): balance/recharge deduction (A), data depletion (B), no internet with an active package (C), balance conflict (D), payment captured but not credited (E), VAS dispute without…","Exact reconciliation in integer cents (e.g. 1,000 − 499 − 60 − 21 = 420); quota and money kept in separate calculations.","Evidence states: SUFFICIENT, PARTIAL or CONFLICTING, decided by rules; conflicts block account changes.","Three allowed actions, each needing an explicit, case-bound confirmation with a 5-minute hash-bound proposal: DEACTIVATEVAS, SENDSETTINGSINSTRUCTIONS, CREATEREVIEWTICKET.","Live operation status: PENDING until the worker records SUCCEEDED or FAILED; pending is never shown as success. Idempotency keys give exactly one account change on retries."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Zeptaz/hutch_resolve/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"83b1be783f804b70f2a458337bb41b2f1202f9af8d921e68c21a02a7a5586ac9","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:28.940Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:28.940Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes